# Legacy sitemap URLs kept alive for Googlebot/Bingbot.
#
# Every sitemap URL that ever appeared in Google Search Console or Bing
# Webmaster Tools 301s to the CURRENT canonical index at /sitemap.xml (served
# by the deterministic Pages Function). Nothing may 404 here: a 404 at a
# *.xml URL is served with the static 404 HTML page, and if that HTML is ever
# parsed as XML (Google does this for previously-submitted sitemap URLs) it
# produces "xmlParseEntityRef: no name" errors in GSC.
#
# Static (exact) rules first, then dynamic (splat) rules — Pages requires
# this ordering. Do NOT add rules that shadow real build outputs:
# sitemap-main-pages*.xml and sitemap-ai-quality-*.xml are real static files.
/sitemap_index.xml       /sitemap.xml  301
/sitemaps.xml            /sitemap.xml  301
/sitemap-index.xml       /sitemap.xml  301

# Retired versioned indexes (…-2026-06-v3.xml etc.) and retired tier /
# priority / programmatic chunk sitemaps from the pre-edge-resolver era.
/sitemap-index-*         /sitemap.xml  301
/sitemap-tier*           /sitemap.xml  301
/sitemap-priority-*      /sitemap.xml  301
/sitemap-programmatic-*  /sitemap.xml  301
